---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Paint Sheen Selection Guide: Flat, Eggshell, Satin vs Semi-Gloss by Room | CalcForDIY"
  description="Master interior paint sheen selection. Learn when to use Flat, Matte, Eggshell, Satin, and Semi-Gloss based on room moisture, wall imperfections, and cleanability."
>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://calcfordiy.com" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Guides", "item": "https://calcfordiy.com/guides" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Paint Sheen Selection Guide", "item": "https://calcfordiy.com/guides/paint-sheen-selection-guide" }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Paint Sheen Selection Guide: Flat, Eggshell, Satin vs Semi-Gloss by Room",
    "description": "Comprehensive architectural painting guide explaining light reflectivity values (LRV), resin solids, moisture durability, and room-by-room sheen recommendations.",
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "CalcForDIY" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "CalcForDIY", "url": "https://calcfordiy.com" },
    "datePublished": "2026-09-02",
    "dateModified": "2026-09-02"
  }
  </script>

  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4 print:hidden">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-blue-600">Guides</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <span>Paint Sheen Guide by Room</span>
  </div>

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-rose-50 border border-rose-200 rounded-full text-rose-800 text-xs font-semibold mb-3">
        <span>🎨 Architectural Coatings &amp; Finishes</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Paint Selection Guide</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-3 tracking-tight">
        Paint Sheen Guide: Flat, Eggshell, Satin, or Semi-Gloss?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        Choosing the wrong paint sheen can ruin an entire paint job. Flat paint in a bathroom will stain and mildew, while semi-gloss on a ceiling will highlight every tape joint flaw. Here is how to select the right sheen for every room.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Interactive Tool Callout -->
    <div class="p-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl mb-8 shadow-xs flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">Calculate how many gallons of paint you need</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600">Our paint calculator subtracts windows and doors to give exact 1-gallon and 5-gallon bucket counts.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/calculators/paint-room" class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white text-xs font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors shadow-2xs">
        <span>Open Paint Calculator</span>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">1. The Sheen vs. Flaw Visibility Trade-Off</h2>
      <p>
        Paint sheen is governed by the ratio of resin binders to pigment solids:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Higher Gloss (Satin, Semi-Gloss):</strong> Contains more resin and less pigment. Creates a hard, non-porous film that repels water and withstands repeated scrubbing, but reflects light like a mirror, highlighting bumps, dents, and poor drywall taping.</li>
        <li><strong>Lower Gloss (Flat, Matte):</strong> Contains high pigment solids that diffuse light in all directions. Completely hides drywall imperfections, but is porous and difficult to wipe clean without burnishing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">2. Room-by-Room Sheen Recommendation Matrix</h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-xs text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-gray-100 text-gray-800 font-bold border-b border-gray-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Room / Surface</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Recommended Sheen</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Gloss Level</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Why It Works</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 text-gray-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Ceilings (All Rooms)</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold text-blue-700">Flat / Dead Flat</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">0% to 3%</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-xs">Diffuses overhead lighting; conceals ceiling joist sag and drywall seams.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50/50">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Living Rooms &amp; Bedrooms</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold text-emerald-700">Eggshell or Matte</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">10% to 20%</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-xs">Soft decorative warmth with enough durability for light wipe-downs.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Hallways &amp; Kids' Playrooms</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold text-purple-700">Satin</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">25% to 35%</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-xs">Withstands backpack scuffs, handprints, and frequent scrubbing.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50/50">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Bathrooms &amp; Kitchens</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold text-purple-700">Satin or Semi-Gloss</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">30% to 50%</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-xs">Moisture-sealed film resists steam, condensation, and cooking grease.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">Doors, Trim &amp; Baseboards</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold text-amber-800">Semi-Gloss</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4">40% to 70%</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-xs">Hard enamel coating resists vacuum strikes, kicks, and chips.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">3. Painting Over High-Gloss Surfaces</h2>
      <p>
        If you are repainting glossy trim or cabinets with a lower-sheen paint, new paint cannot bond mechanically to the slick surface. You must scuff-sand the gloss with 180-grit sandpaper or apply an acrylic bonding primer (e.g. Zinsser 1-2-3 or Stix) to prevent future peeling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Workflows & Calculators -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related Building Workflows &amp; Tools</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <a href="/calculators/paint-room" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-400 bg-white hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-600 mb-1">CALCULATOR</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-sm">Room Paint Calculator</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Calculate gallons for walls, trim, and ceilings.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/projects/room-accent-wall" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-400 bg-white hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-600 mb-1">PROJECT WORKFLOW</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-sm">Room Accent Wall Hub</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Coordinating paint colors with millwork and trim.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/calculators/drywall-primer-sealer" class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-400 bg-white hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-600 mb-1">CALCULATOR</div>
          <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-sm">Drywall Primer Calculator</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Estimate primer sealer gallons before painting.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

</Layout>
